fastest, deepest 100 metres ever, with Kerley taking bronze in 9.81, as Simbine settled for fourth with a South African Record 9.82. Best-ever-marks for place were set for places 4-5-6-7-8, with Seville finishing eighth in 9.91."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Preliminary Round"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1328"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/2104512"} "Noah Lyles"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "10.04 (2 h3)"] [:td {} "9.83 (2 h1)"] [:td {} "9.784 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "915"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/150190"} "Kishane Thompson"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JAM"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JAM.png"}] "JAM"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "10.00 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "9.80 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "9.789 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1319"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/147327"} "Fred Kerley"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "9.97 (1 h8)"] [:td {} "9.84 (2 h3)"] [:td {} "9.81 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1191"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/135668"} "Akani Simbine"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/RSA"} [:img {:style "padding-right